    "body": "### Description\nIn my app I want to move from using `newMdkUnencrypted()` to using `newMdk()` but I can't get it to work. `newMdkUnencrypted()` and `newMdkWithKey()` work fine.\n\nI tried to call it like this but this won't work because I need to set up keystore first:\n`mdk = newMdk(filesDir.resolve(\"mdk.db\").absolutePath, packageName, \"mdk.db.key.default\", null)`\n\nFollowing the [encrypted-storage-plan.md](https://github.com/marmot-protocol/mdk/blob/master/crates/mdk-core/docs/encrypted-storage-plan.md#platform-store-initialization) guide for Android, I then added this to a new file in my project to setup keystore:\n``` Kotlin\npackage io.crates.keyring\n\nimport android.content.Context\n\nclass Keyring {\n    companion object {\n        init {\n            System.loadLibrary(\"mdk_uniffi\")\n        }\n\n        external fun setAndroidKeyringCredentialBuilder(context: Context)\n    }\n}\n```\n\nand then I call `Keyring.setAndroidKeyringCredentialBuilder(this)` before calling `newMdk()`. But when I run it, I get a crash with this error:\n```\njava.lang.UnsatisfiedLinkError: No implementation found for void io.crates.keyring.Keyring$Companion.setAndroidKeyringCredentialBuilder(android.content.Context) (tried Java_io_crates_keyring_Keyring_00024Companion_setAndroidKeyringCredentialBuilder and Java_io_crates_keyring_Keyring_00024Companion_setAndroidKeyringCredentialBuilder__Landroid_content_Context_2)\n```\n\n### Details\n- Tested on Android API 9\n- I tried disabling minify, but it's still the same error",
